<title>AUSTRALIA: Suncorp-Metway sells unit to AMP Society.</title>
<headline>Suncorp-Metway sells unit to AMP Society.</headline>
<dateline>BRISBANE 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Queensland state government-controlled Suncorp-Metway Ltd said on Friday that it had sold its superannuation administration business to the Australian Mutual Provident Society (AMP).</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Suncorp-Metway, an insurance and banking group, said the Suncorp Advisors and Administrators (SAA) unit which had been sold to AMP currently administers 25 industry funds throughout Australia.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
